<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Best selling price for the greatest profit</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(it=1)"]]Mwanajuma sells cups of sugarcane juice at her stall in Mombasa. Each cup costs Ksh \({@c0@}\) to make. At a price of Ksh \(p\) a cup, she sells \({@N0-k0*p@}\) cups a day.[[elif test="is(it=2)"]]Otieno sells chapatis at his kibanda in Kisumu. Each chapati costs Ksh \({@c0@}\) to make. At a price of Ksh \(p\) each, he sells \({@N0-k0*p@}\) chapatis a day.[[else]]Chebet sells cups of yoghurt at her dairy kiosk in Nakuru. Each cup costs Ksh \({@c0@}\) to make. At a price of Ksh \(p\) a cup, she sells \({@N0-k0*p@}\) cups a day.[[/if]]</p><p>(a) Write the daily profit \(P\) (in Ksh) in terms of \(p\).</p><div>\(P =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the price that gives the greatest daily profit.</p><div>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the greatest daily profit.</p><div>Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Profit = (profit on each item) \(\times\) (number sold).</p><p>(a) \(P = {@Pm@} = {@expand(Pm)@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\dfrac{dP}{dp} = {@diff(expand(Pm),p)@} = 0\) when \(p = {@pb@}\). \(\dfrac{d^2P}{dp^2} = {@-2*k0@} \lt 0\), so this is a maximum: the best price is Ksh \({@pb@}\).</p><p>(c) At that price \({@nb@}\) are sold a day, and \(P = {@pb-c0@} \times {@nb@} = [[if test="is(Pb>=10000)"]]{#floor(Pb/1000)#}\,{#floor(mod(Pb,1000)/100)#}{#floor(mod(Pb,100)/10)#}{#mod(Pb,10)#}[[else]]{#Pb#}[[/if]]\): the greatest daily profit is Ksh \([[if test="is(Pb>=10000)"]]{#floor(Pb/1000)#}\,{#floor(mod(Pb,1000)/100)#}{#floor(mod(Pb,100)/10)#}{#mod(Pb,10)#}[[else]]{#Pb#}[[/if]]\).</p><p>The takings alone, \({@Rm@}\), would be greatest at Ksh \({@pr@}\), a different price: the cost of making each item moves the best price up.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_p(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [p])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Use p as the only letter in your answer.";
/* Design: a cost per item is included, so profit, not takings, is maximised. Question variables never use p, which the learner types. it: 1 juice, 2 chapati, 3 yoghurt. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 9, Example 5. */
L: [[1,20,300,2],[2,10,240,4],[3,40,560,4],[1,30,400,4],[2,12,300,6],[3,50,600,3],[1,24,360,3],[2,8,200,5],[3,36,520,4],[1,16,280,4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
it: L[ix][1]; c0: L[ix][2]; N0: L[ix][3]; k0: L[ix][4];
Pm: (p-c0)*(N0-k0*p);
pb: (N0/k0+c0)/2; Pb: ev(Pm,p=pb); nb: N0-k0*pb;
Rm: p*(N0-k0*p); Lm: (c0-p)*(N0-k0*p);
pr: N0/(2*k0); pz: N0/k0;
Rmax: pr*(N0-k0*pr); Rb: pb*(N0-k0*pb);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
