  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Differentiation II: best selling price for the greatest profit</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.1: Model daily profit from a cost per item and a linear demand, and find the best price and the greatest profit.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Example 5 in Section D of Chapter 9 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: a cost per item is added so that profit, not takings, is maximised, with Kenyan contexts and new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
